From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Fursund <jens@spectralcompute.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the build set the collective unroll

ncclCollUnroll takes the collectives' unroll from the compute
capability alone, and ncclShmemDynamicSize the dynamic shared memory
per block from the unroll: 82240 B from sm_80 on (unroll 8). The unroll
is a template argument of the device code, so it can't follow the
device's limit at run time. A device that reports sm_80 or newer with
less shared memory per block fails every communicator init ("dynamic
smem 82240 exceeds device/fn maxSharedMem"): AMD GPUs through SCALE,
which reports sm_89, have 64 KiB.

Add a COLL_UNROLL make option, as MAX_EXT_NET_PLUGINS is, which defines
NCCL_COLL_UNROLL for host and device code, and return it from
ncclCollUnroll when it is set. Without it nothing changes: unroll 8
from sm_80, 6 on sm_120, 4 below sm_80.

Checked with g++ against device.h: by default, ncclCollUnroll(890) is
8 and ncclShmemDynamicSize(890) 82240; with COLL_UNROLL=4 they are 4
and 41280, which fits in 64 KiB. SCALE's NCCL builds have used unroll 4
on AMD GPUs, with nccl-tests passing every collective.
---
 makefiles/common.mk  |    7 +++++++
 src/include/device.h |    5 +++++
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/makefiles/common.mk b/makefiles/common.mk
index 75cbf6b..160563c 100644
--- a/makefiles/common.mk
+++ b/makefiles/common.mk
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ RDMA_CORE ?= 0
 NET_PROFILER ?= 0
 MLX5DV ?= 0
 MAX_EXT_NET_PLUGINS ?= 0
+COLL_UNROLL ?= 0
 EMIT_LLVM_IR ?= 0
 
 NVCC ?= $(CUDA_HOME)/bin/nvcc
@@ -163,6 +164,12 @@ ifneq ($(MAX_EXT_NET_PLUGINS), 0)
 CXXFLAGS += -DNCCL_NET_MAX_PLUGINS=$(MAX_EXT_NET_PLUGINS)
 endif
 
+# Collective unroll for devices with less shared memory per block than their compute capability implies.
+ifneq ($(COLL_UNROLL), 0)
+CXXFLAGS  += -DNCCL_COLL_UNROLL=$(COLL_UNROLL)
+NVCUFLAGS += -DNCCL_COLL_UNROLL=$(COLL_UNROLL)
+endif
+
 CXXFLAGS += -DDOCA_VERBS_USE_CUDA_WRAPPER -DDOCA_VERBS_USE_NET_WRAPPER
 NVCUFLAGS += -DDOCA_VERBS_USE_CUDA_WRAPPER -DDOCA_VERBS_USE_NET_WRAPPER
 
diff --git a/src/include/device.h b/src/include/device.h
index e55d009..bf30968 100644
--- a/src/include/device.h
+++ b/src/include/device.h
@@ -522,8 +522,13 @@ __host__ __device__ constexpr int ncclCalcUnroll(int bytePerPack, int insns, int
 // side code can elide passing the arch for brevity.
 
 __host__ __device__ constexpr int ncclCollUnroll(int cudaArch = NCCL_CUDA_ARCH) {
+#ifdef NCCL_COLL_UNROLL
+  // Set by the build (COLL_UNROLL) for devices with less shared memory per block than cudaArch implies.
+  return NCCL_COLL_UNROLL;
+#else
   // Our collective unroll should move to the same bytes&insns model as NVLS.
   return cudaArch >= 800 ? (cudaArch / 100 == 12 ? 6 : 8) : 4;
+#endif
 }
 
 __host__ __device__ constexpr int ncclNvlsUnrollBytes(int cudaArch = NCCL_CUDA_ARCH) { return 4*16; }
